        <history>
          <p>Inspired by the garden of Delius's own house at Grez-sur-Loing in France, this orchestral rhapsody is among the most personal of his tone poems, evoking the sounds and colours of a specific, real place rather than a literary or folk source. Delius revised the work in 1911 with the addition of quiet vocal parts, later removed in performance practice.</p>
